    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Goal review — cold start, sweep a window, prioritise against stated goals",
      "prov:value": "Authored 2026-09-20 from a live session (bean `mgta`, issue #578): the owner\nasked for \"a synopsis of all that was active in the last 4 hrs — what is\nclosed, what is open, what needs to be done (work effort)\", classified\nagainst three goals, then asked that the interaction become this skill. The\nnumbers in this file are that session's measurements, kept as provenance for\nthe rules; they are not a description of the repository today.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mgta",
        "#578",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Goal review — cold start, sweep a window, prioritise against stated goals",
      "prov:value": "**And a number is not the only thing that goes stale. A sentence like *\"the\nAPI may not be able to see them: on DATE eight lookups returned not found\"*\nwelds a **present-tense capability claim** to its dated evidence, and a\ndisclaimer about numbers does not reach the claim — a reader takes the first\nclause as guidance and never re-tests it. So in this file every dated\nobservation is **labelled as one**, and every instruction is written in the\npresent tense as something to DO. Where the two have since disagreed, both are\nkept: the observation with its date, and what re-measurement found. Bean\n`8nzu`, opened after this skill's own axis 1 sent its first reader the wrong\nway.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8nzu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Inputs — four, all stated before the first read",
      "prov:value": "Bean `tjj6`,\nmeasured 2026-09-24: the owner ran `/goal-review 1d` with no goals while the\nstore carried three goal milestones (`vuip`, `p5wm`, `yg29`) — exactly the\nobjects §\"Goals that are not in the store are a gap\" exists to create — and the\nreview built no queue, dropping the one input the store could supply. So with\nno goals given, list the open milestones (`beans list -t milestone`), each\ntitle **verbatim**, and offer them as the queue basis in the closing question.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tjj6",
        "bean p5wm",
        "bean yg29",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Cold start — before any durable read",
      "prov:value": "On 2026-09-20 it named a path that had moved in\n  the repository split, in both `AGENTS.md` and the README.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "**Reading the listing — measured, bean `4dxv` (2026-09-24). It is ordered by\n**creation, not activity**: a 40-row page held 22 sessions updated in a 1-day\nwindow interleaved with ones last active weeks earlier, and page 2 held none. Stopping at the first page with no *in-window* row is right for\nthat reason and no other; a reader who does not know the order either stops at\npage 1 or pages forever.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4dxv",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "*Dated observation, 2026-09-20, kept as provenance and NOT as a capability\nclaim:* eight lookups by id returned *not found* and the listing showed only\nthe asking session. **Contradicted 2026-09-21**, when the same listing returned\nseven siblings with their statuses — and with four sessions' pending questions,\nwhich the trailer route cannot reach at all. The earlier sentence here asserted\nthat the API \"may not be able to see them\", welding a present-tense claim to\nits dated evidence, and a reader who followed it skipped the query and missed\nthe sweep's headline. Bean `8nzu`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8nzu",
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "For each open one, read the merge state, the CI outcome on the current head,\nthe last comment, the reviews, and whether the body or last comment carries\na question to the owner — quote the question. \"Green\" means every check on\nthe head passed; a head with no checks is not green (bean `3pqn`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3pqn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "On 2026-09-20 that was 43 of 60, and 38 of the 43 had last been\n  touched by one bulk move hours earlier. `in-progress` records a claim; it\n  does not record that anyone is working ([`bean-coordination`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md)\n  §\"A claim is branch-local\"). The store is committed per branch,\n  so a long-running proposal can carry an entire epic the default branch has\n  never seen (13 of 14 items for one goal, that day).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "A session\n  fetches `origin/main` and fast-forwards its own branch; the local `main`\n  just sits there. Bean `065p`: written as `git diff main..origin/<branch>`,\n  with local `main` **2655** commits stale, every branch appeared to carry\n  **566-573** unmerged beans where the true count against `origin/main` was\n  **1**. Off by ~570x, and in the direction that manufactures a crisis — an\n  agent reading that concludes the work plan has fractured across branches and\n  starts reconciling something intact. Re-measured in a different container\n  2026-09-27: **3277** commits stale, so the trap grows rather than ages out. Both spellings are grammatical and one is silently wrong by two orders of\n  magnitude, which is why the ref is named here rather than left to the reader.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 065p",
        "2026-09-27"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "```sh\n  # Resolve the default branch, then FALL BACK — `origin/HEAD` is unset in some\n  # clones, measured 2026-09-27: without the fallback this exits 128 in exactly\n  # the container the check is for.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-27"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "An explicit refspec, not a bare `git fetch origin $DB`: the bare form updates\n  `refs/remotes/origin/$DB` only when `remote.origin.fetch` happens to cover it,\n  and exits 0 when it does not (bean `9giz`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9giz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "Bean\n  `x6lu`, measured 2026-09-24, and NOT the same trap as `065p` above: with a\n  fresh `origin/main`, `git diff --diff-filter=A origin/main...origin/<branch>\n  -- beans/defs` listed **131** added beans for a branch 822 commits behind;\n  by id, **1** was absent from main. `A...B` diffs against the **merge\n  base**, which predates everything main gained since — so the count\n  inflates with how far behind the branch is, the same symptom as a stale\n  ref from a different cause. Across that day's 19 unmerged branches: 152 by\n  file diff, 20 unique by id.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean x6lu",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "*Dated observation,\n2026-09-20:* 54 proposals merged and 2 issues changed — which this file\npreviously turned into \"expect this axis to be thin where work is bean-driven\",\nan instruction to under-read it. **Measured 2026-09-21: 30 issues touched, 23\nnewly opened. The inversion was not an accident — the repository adopted a\nround summary per bean and an issue per piece of work, so the skill's own\nsubject changed underneath the number. Bean `8nzu`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8nzu",
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "Bean `52rd`, measured\n2026-09-24: `check:ci-health` reads the last 100 runs and says so — \"100\nrecent run(s) spanning 13.4h\" — against a 24h window, leaving the first ~10.6h\nwith no CI verdict at all. The tool is honest; the easy reading, \"main is\ngreen\", is not.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 52rd",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The six axes, and what each one can and cannot tell you",
      "prov:value": "**Where a check fails, sidecars and generated files are the first suspect**:\none proposal that day was red only because a QA sidecar had not been\nregenerated after its skill was edited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Classify against the goals — judgement, marked as judgement",
      "prov:value": "Read dependencies from item bodies, not from the\n   `blocked_by` field alone: on 2026-09-20 no item on one goal's path carried\n   the field, and every dependency was prose.\n3.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Output — three parts, in this order",
      "prov:value": "Create the item with the measurement in its body and\nthe rule it concerns named; parent it to the process epic; that is the\n\"bean up\" the owner asked for."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rules",
      "prov:value": "Bean `pesg`, and it is measured twice over. `bun run cat health` reported **one**\n   orphaned staging preview; a review re-implemented the slug rule inline\n   (`[^a-zA-Z0-9]+` where `feature-staging.yml` preserves `.`, `_` and `-`),\n   reported **three**, and the owner authorised deleting \"the 3 orphans\". Two of\n   the three were LIVE previews for open PRs #1337 and #914 — caught only\n   because directory sizes were measured before deleting. `stagingSlug` was\n   already exported from `schemas/sdlc/staging.ts` and already differentially tested\n   against the real `sed`, one import away. Independently, 2026-09-27: an agent\n   extending `check:anchor-names` probed its own narrower file set instead of\n   quoting the check's own count, wrote **25** invisible ascents into a docblock\n   where the check said **75**, and had to retract it in the same change. Two\n   agents, two subjects, one move.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean pesg",
        "#1337",
        "#914",
        "2026-09-27"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rules",
      "prov:value": "Several items that day were blocked only in name — the ruling was already\n   in a sibling's body."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read the published survey before deriving one",
      "prov:value": "**`bun run cat survey:owed` first. Bean `6ptx`: eight sessions ran in the same\nminute and seven were doing this same sweep, over the same ~2435-commit window. Authored commits on `main` that day: **one**. Throughput did not fall because\nthe work ran out — 243 beans were open — it fell because everybody was reading,\nand none of them could see the other seven.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 6ptx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read the published survey before deriving one",
      "prov:value": "That is a\nfirst-class answer: a survey of four of six axes is useful, and a reader must\nbe able to tell which two it says nothing about. Recording only what you did\nlets a partial survey read as a complete one, which is `1xhc` — absence taken\nfor a clean result."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/goal-review.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read the published survey before deriving one",
      "prov:value": "This does not claim the window and does not divide the axes between sessions —\nthose were considered and not chosen."
    }
  ]
